  "name": "Robot Bark Drop",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A one-shot robot bark: every note starts with a bright, ring-modulated metallic bite that dives and settles into a hollow growl over a clean sine sub, so stuttered playing becomes a machine-gun of barks. Play: short, separated F1, G1 and A#1 notes at 140-150 BPM, or tap eighths and sixteenths; the bite re-fires on every new key press. Macros: Bite brightens the ring-mod, Dive deepens the pitch drop, Metal adds ring-modulation and Drive pushes the diode distortion.",
